    "meta": {
        "difficulty": "beginner",
        "notes": "A birdhouse from one cedar 1x6: the front and back are dog-eared to a 45° peak, the right roof panel laps over the left at the ridge, and the sides stop short of the roof to leave a vent under the eaves. The 1 1/4\" hole suits chickadees and wrens. The floor sits 1/4\" up to drain.",
